WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.400
More than three million people have
signed up to storm Area 51 in September

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.120
to "see them aliens". There's probably not
any men in black working with

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.809
extraterrestrials in the Nevada desert,
what's actually going on at Area 51 is

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:20.310
even cooler. The Air Force originally
bought Area 51 to test the famous U-2

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:24.390
reconnaissance plane, often the source of
UFO sightings during the Cold War. It was

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.470
later used to develop America's first
operational stealth aircraft, the F-117

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.500
Nighthawk. The secretive southwest
training ranges have grown significantly

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.280
over the years, and today they're working
on bleeding-edge aircraft tech for the

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.590
US military, like the new B-21 stealth
bomber and the X-37B space plane. These

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.430
ranges also helped to develop the RQ-170
stealth drone — used to find bin Laden —and

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:49.920
the RQ-180, it's successor, of which no
pictures exist. Area 51 and its cousins

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.850
are also crucial to testing a whole host
of revolutionary, unmanned combat drones

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.800
to work with our current fighters — the
F-35 in F-22. So when the motherships do

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.520
show up and Bill Pullman leads us into
battle, humanity's best chance of victory

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.660
lies in the aircraft being tested at
Area 51 today.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:12.020
What's the coolest thing the Air Force is working on today? Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know what

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.570
other topics you'd like our scholars to
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.790
and subscribe for more research and
videos from AEI.

